.TH "GLESHA-LIST" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-list \- list known backup sets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha list\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the name and ID of every set in local state. A set whose catalog has not been opened yet is shown as '(locked catalog)'; refer to it by its ID.
.PP
To find sets created on another computer, run 'glesha catalog sync' first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-remote
Search \-\-from remotes (deprecated: use catalog sync).
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Remotes to search with \-\-remote.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha list
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-catalog (1),
.BR glesha\-status (1)
